# A sample fact pack (.facts form): one declarative fact per line.
# `# scope: <id>` sets the scope for the lines that follow it, until the next directive.
# Load it:  neuron import app.db examples/preloads/kb.facts
# Or seed an MCP server:  NEURON_MCP_PRELOAD=examples/preloads/kb.facts neuron-mcp

# scope: solar-system
The Sun contains about 99.8 percent of the mass of the solar system.
Jupiter is the largest planet in the solar system.
Mercury is the closest planet to the Sun.
A year on Neptune lasts about 165 Earth years.

# scope: chemistry
Water is composed of two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom.
Table salt is sodium chloride.
The atomic number of carbon is 6.
Helium is the second most abundant element in the universe.

# scope: computing
TCP provides reliable, ordered delivery; UDP does not.
A hash map offers average constant-time lookups.
The DNS system resolves domain names to IP addresses.
